ands; imported fertilisers; and bagged gypsum under the FACT Gypsum brand. It also provides caprolactam, such as benzene, sulphur, ammonia, and carbon dioxide for use in manufacturing nylon tyre cords, nylon filament yarns, and engineering plastics, etc. for the textile and automobile industries; and by-products comprising anhydrous ammonia, cyclohexanone, soda ash, gypsum, sulphuric acid, and carbon dioxide. In addition, the company imports fertilizers, including muriate of potash and others; and offers various services for farmers. Further, it engages in engineering consultancy and design; and fabrication and erection of industrial equipment activities. The Fertilisers and Chemicals Travancore Limited was incorporated in 1943 and is headquartered in Kochi, India.","beta":0.266,"sharesOutstanding":647071974,"marketCap":489057026048,"priceToBook":36.6431,"enterpriseToEbitda":641.319,"dividendYield":0.0,"heldPercentInsiders":0.0,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.0009,"earningsGrowth":0.906,"revenueGrowth":-0.102,"website":"https://www.fact.co.in","fullTimeEmployees":1481,"recommendationKey":"none","financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":null,"revenue":{"0q":{"avg":0.0,"low":0.0,"high":0.0,"numberOfAnalysts":0.0},"+1q":{"avg":0.0,"low":0.0,"high":0.0,"numberOfAnalysts":0.0},"0y":{"avg":0.0,"low":0.0,"high":0.0,"numberOfAnalysts":0.0},"+1y":{"avg":0.0,"low":0.0,"high":0.0,"numberOfAnalysts":0.0}},"growth":{"0q":{"stockTrend":null,"indexTrend":0.3015},"+1q":{"stockTrend":null,"indexTrend":0.276},"0y":{"stockTrend":null,"indexTrend":0.3365},"+1y":{"stockTrend":null,"indexTrend":0.1696},"LTG":{"stockTrend":null,"indexTrend":0.122}},"next_earnings":[]}}